  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the operator, I want one slide in the periodic report deck that covers every end-of-M4 audit, so that I can see at a glance which audits are done and how their findings are being handled. (Operator, 2026-11-18, when #775 and #866 were launched.)\n\n### Scope\n\n- One slide in the deck built by `tooling/roadmap/weekly/build.py` (French, like the rest of the deck).\n- One row per end-of-M4 audit: #774 performance, #775 quality, #836 duplicates, #866 UI/UX (HIG, WWDC), #326 audit of outside contributions. LOT-164 #254 (the parity gate) may appear as the last step.\n- Per audit: its status (not started / running / done, from the review issue's status and state), the number of findings (issues carrying its `m4-review: <name>` label), and the closure rate of those findings (closed / total), with open findings split by status (`on-hold` awaiting triage, `ready`, `claimed`).\n- Data from the tracker only (labels and states), reusing the label prefix `m4-review: ` that `tooling/roadmap/weekly/counts.py` already reads. Nothing names or ranks a person.\n\n### Blocked by\n\n#775 #866\n\n### When\n\nThe slide is added once #775 and #866 are done (operator). A version that shows « non démarré » for the other audits is fine.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A test in `scripts/tests/test_roadmap.py` pins the counts from a fixture of labelled issues (findings per audit, closure rate, on-hold count).\n- [ ] The slide renders through `shot.js` with no overflow; a screenshot in the PR.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
